  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe combination of clear skies under light east to southeasterly \nflow has resulted in the proliferation of dense fog through southern \nand central Michigan, and to a lesser extent across the Thumb. The \nfavorable flow has brought about better moisture advection derived \nfrom Lake Erie inland, where continued advection along with gentle \nupsloping will see dense fog expand west and northwest through \ncentral MI. This will continue to promote fog across Monroe and \nLenawee counties, where a dense fog advisory is in effect until 10 \nAM EDT. Portions of western Washtenaw, the Tri-Cities and Thumb will\nlikely see periodic fog, possibly dense at times, through daybreak, \nwith sunshine then works the lift and scour out fog through the \nremaining morning hours. \n\nThe familiar persistence forecast will again take hold today as high \npressure sits over the Great Lakes, which will be reinforced through \nFriday as a longwave ridge expands through the Plains and \nMidwest/Great Lakes. Dry weather and above normal temperatures \ncontinue as a result through the weekend. Daytime highs will return \ninto the upper 60s today and tomorrow and may make a push into the \n70s by tomorrow afternoon. A very subtle decrease in highs (low to \nmid 60s) will be likely Friday with northeast flow coming off the \nlake, but as the aforementioned high pressure system starts to \ndepart into the western Atlantic, low-level flow re-orients south to \nsouthwesterly, resulting in the gentle uptick in waa  pushing highs \nback in the mid to upper 60s. Fog, dense at times, remains highly \nsensitive to wind direction as shallow lake moisture advection has \nbeen the main driver of recent events. Tomorrow morning fog is a \npossibility under clear skies, but the unfavorable flow lowers \nconfidence relative to today. Friday morning will be much more \nconducive to advective fog given the light east to northeast flow \noff of Lake Huron and Saginaw Bay. Patchy to areas of dense fog will \nbe possible through the Tri-Cities and Thumb with lowered confidence \nfor the degree of expansion inland. Outside of morning fog concerns, \ndry and sunny weather continues through the weekend.",
